      "fileLayoutStrategyId": "single-file",
      "text": {
        "source": "",
        "sourceLanguageId": "",
        "initialization": "",
        "initializationLanguageId": "",
        "specification": "WebServer — the HTTP/1.1 transport of a Wirecraft C17 dataflow server, as a pluggable component.\n\nPORTS (published through Exteriors; see docs/design/components.md)\n- request  (output, ReqRep): every accepted, fully read request. Exactly one consumer link.\n- response (input,  ReqRep): completed responses; set response.status, content_type and body.\n  Any number of consumer links. The packet must keep the id, connection and request strings\n  of the request it answers.\nThe component owns accepting, reading, rendering, writing, logging and freeing; the consumer\nowns routing and response bodies.\n\nCONFIGURATION (environment, read once at startup)\nWEBSERVER_PORT (default 8080), WEBSERVER_BIND_ANY=1 (listen on 0.0.0.0, default 127.0.0.1),\nWEBSERVER_MAX_REQUESTS (exit after N resolved requests; default unlimited).\n\nFLOW\nsocket_accept --request--> [consumer] --response--> socket_respond --rendered--> socket_accept.\nWhile a request is in flight its pending copy circulates on awaitResponseLoop; socket_accept\nmatches each rendered response to it by id, writes the reply and closes the connection.\n\nOWNERSHIP OF ReqRep STRINGS (packets are copied by value)\n- The pending copy on awaitResponseLoop owns id, request.header and request.body.\n- Consumer copies only borrow them. The consumer allocates response.body (or leaves it NULL);\n  socket_respond allocates response.header. content_type must point to a string literal.\n- socket_accept frees all of them exactly once when it resolves the request.\n\nLIMITS AND ERRORS\nHeader ≤ 8 KiB (else 431), body ≤ 64 KiB by Content-Length (else 413), 2 s receive timeout\n(408 when nothing arrives, 400 on a truncated request). These connections are answered by the\nlibrary and never reach the request port. Allocation or socket failures end the run with\nTHREADWORK_ERROR; the process exits non-zero.\n\nEXECUTION MODEL, SHUTDOWN AND LOG\nOne connection is accepted per tick; reading blocks up to 2 s per connection. After shutdown\nsocket_accept stops accepting, resolves every pending request, then closes the listener. It\nprints one access-log line per resolved request: \"<id> <method> <path> <status> <body bytes>\".\nStatic state (sequence, limit, the listener) allows one instance per program.\n",
        "specificationLanguageId": "markdown",
        "tests": "Compile and run through a consumer such as examples/webserver.orch; see its Tests section.",
        "testsLanguageId": "json",
        "aiInstructions": "",
        "aiInstructionsLanguageId": "markdown"
      },
      "binaryContent": null,
