    {
      "id": "cf346fce-593a-4903-b9ac-51afa8814a9a",
      "name": "lib_http_server",
      "kind": "Processor",
      "parentId": "root",
      "children": [],
      "incomingLinks": [
        "95f28f57-d01a-4781-bc3c-ecca3987459d"
      ],
      "outgoingLinks": [
        "32e5289b-5f71-4d77-a5a5-e0a8b107bc63",
        "992f1269-5aa2-4929-91a3-5745c23f6cb9"
      ],
      "layout": {
        "x": -204.98622018170352,
        "y": 735.9605822627288,
        "width": 200.0,
        "height": 70.0,
        "closedWidth": 200.0,
        "closedHeight": 70.0,
        "openWidth": 200.0,
        "openHeight": 70.0,
        "isExpanded": true
      },
      "fileLayoutStrategyId": "none",
      "text": {
        "source": "/* HTTP/1.1 helpers for the WebServer network. Lent to consumers as `libhttp`. */\n#include <sys/types.h>\n#include <sys/socket.h>\n#include <sys/select.h> /* struct timeval for SO_RCVTIMEO */\n#include <netinet/in.h>\n#include <fcntl.h>\n#include <poll.h>\n#include <errno.h>\n\n#define HTTP_MAX_HEADER 8192\n#define HTTP_MAX_BODY 65536\n\n/* Listening socket shared by the http_* functions; -1 when closed. */\nstatic int http_listener = -1;\n\n/* Heap copy of `length` bytes plus a terminating NUL, or NULL. */\nstatic char *http_copy(const char *text, size_t length)\n{\n    char *copy = (char *)malloc(length + 1U);\n\n    if (copy != NULL) {\n        memcpy(copy, text, length);\n        copy[length] = '\\0';\n    }\n    return copy;\n}\n\nstatic int http_lower(int c)\n{\n    return (c >= 'A' && c <= 'Z') ? c - 'A' + 'a' : c;\n}\n\n/* Non-negative integer value of a header field (case-insensitive name), or -1. */\nstatic long http_header_number(const char *header, const char *name)\n{\n    size_t length = strlen(name);\n    const char *line = strstr(header, \"\\r\\n\");\n\n    while (line != NULL && line[2] != '\\0' && !(line[2] == '\\r' && line[3] == '\\n')) {\n        const char *field = line + 2;\n        size_t i = 0U;\n\n        while (i < length && field[i] != '\\0'\n            && http_lower((unsigned char)field[i]) == http_lower((unsigned char)name[i])) {\n            i++;\n        }\n        if (i == length && field[i] == ':') {\n            char *end = NULL;\n            long value = strtol(field + i + 1, &end, 10);\n            return (end != field + i + 1 && value >= 0) ? value : -1;\n        }\n        line = strstr(field, \"\\r\\n\");\n    }\n    return -1;\n}\n\nconst char *http_status_text(int status)\n{\n    switch (status) {\n    case 200: return \"OK\";\n    case 400: return \"Bad Request\";\n    case 404: return \"Not Found\";\n    case 405: return \"Method Not Allowed\";\n    case 408: return \"Request Timeout\";\n    case 413: return \"Content Too Large\";\n    case 431: return \"Request Header Fields Too Large\";\n    case 500: return \"Internal Server Error\";\n    default: return \"Unknown\";\n    }\n}\n\n/* Writes every byte, retrying on EINTR and never raising SIGPIPE; 0 on success. */\nstatic int http_write_all(int connection, const char *data, size_t length)\n{\n    while (length > 0U) {\n#ifdef MSG_NOSIGNAL\n        ssize_t written = send(connection, data, length, MSG_NOSIGNAL);\n#else\n        ssize_t written = send(connection, data, length, 0);\n#endif\n        if (written < 0) {\n            if (errno == EINTR) {\n                continue;\n            }\n            return -1;\n        }\n        data += written;\n        length -= (size_t)written;\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\n\n/* Answers a connection that never became a request, then closes it. */\nstatic void http_reject(int connection, int status)\n{\n    char reply[256];\n    const char *text = http_status_text(status);\n    int length = snprintf(reply, sizeof(reply),\n        \"HTTP/1.1 %d %s\\r\\nContent-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8\\r\\nContent-Length: %zu\\r\\n\"\n        \"Connection: close\\r\\nServer: Wirecraft-WebServer/0.1\\r\\n\\r\\n%d %s\\n\",\n        status, text, strlen(text) + 5U, status, text);\n\n    if (length > 0) {\n        (void)http_write_all(connection, reply, (size_t)length);\n    }\n    /* Closing with unread request bytes would reset the connection and lose the reply:\n       finish sending, then discard what the client still sends (bounded by the 2 s timeout). */\n    if (shutdown(connection, SHUT_WR) == 0) {\n        char discard[4096];\n        size_t drained = 0U;\n        ssize_t count;\n\n        while (drained < (size_t)HTTP_MAX_BODY\n               && (count = recv(connection, discard, sizeof(discard), 0)) > 0) {\n            drained += (size_t)count;\n        }\n    }\n    close(connection);\n}\n\nint http_listen(int port, int any_address)\n{\n    struct sockaddr_in address;\n    int enable = 1;\n    int flags;\n\n    if (port <= 0 || port > 65535) {\n        return -1;\n    }\n    http_listener = socket(AF_INET, SOCK_STREAM, 0);\n    if (http_listener < 0) {\n        return -1;\n    }\n    (void)setsockopt(http_listener, SOL_SOCKET, SO_REUSEADDR, &enable, sizeof(enable));\n    memset(&address, 0, sizeof(address));\n    address.sin_family = AF_INET;\n    address.sin_port = htons((uint16_t)port);\n    address.sin_addr.s_addr = htonl(any_address ? INADDR_ANY : INADDR_LOOPBACK);\n    flags = fcntl(http_listener, F_GETFL, 0);\n    if (bind(http_listener, (struct sockaddr *)&address, sizeof(address)) != 0\n        || listen(http_listener, 64) != 0 || flags < 0\n        || fcntl(http_listener, F_SETFL, flags | O_NONBLOCK) != 0) {\n        close(http_listener);\n        http_listener = -1;\n        return -1;\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\n\nint http_wait(int timeout_ms)\n{\n    struct pollfd watched;\n\n    if (http_listener < 0) {\n        return 0;\n    }\n    watched.fd = http_listener;\n    watched.events = POLLIN;\n    watched.revents = 0;\n    return poll(&watched, 1, timeout_ms) > 0 && (watched.revents & POLLIN) != 0;\n}\n\nvoid http_close(void)\n{\n    if (http_listener >= 0) {\n        close(http_listener);\n        http_listener = -1;\n    }\n}\n\nint http_accept(unsigned long sequence, ReqRep *out)\n{\n    static char buffer[HTTP_MAX_HEADER + HTTP_MAX_BODY + 1];\n    struct timeval timeout = { 2, 0 };\n    size_t received = 0U;\n    size_t header_length;\n    size_t total;\n    char *end = NULL;\n    char id[32];\n    long body_length;\n    int connection = accept(http_listener, NULL, NULL);\n\n    if (connection < 0) {\n        return (errno == EAGAIN || errno == EWOULDBLOCK || errno == EINTR) ? 0 : -1;\n    }\n    (void)setsockopt(connection, SOL_SOCKET, SO_RCVTIMEO, &timeout, sizeof(timeout));\n    while (end == NULL) {\n        ssize_t count;\n\n        if (received >= HTTP_MAX_HEADER) {\n            http_reject(connection, 431);\n            return 0;\n        }\n        count = recv(connection, buffer + received, HTTP_MAX_HEADER - received, 0);\n        if (count < 0 && errno == EINTR) {\n            continue;\n        }\n        if (count <= 0) {\n            http_reject(connection, received == 0U && count < 0 ? 408 : 400);\n            return 0;\n        }\n        received += (size_t)count;\n        buffer[received] = '\\0';\n        end = strstr(buffer, \"\\r\\n\\r\\n\");\n    }\n    header_length = (size_t)(end - buffer) + 4U;\n    body_length = http_header_number(buffer, \"Content-Length\");\n    if (body_length < 0) {\n        body_length = 0;\n    }\n    if (body_length > HTTP_MAX_BODY) {\n        http_reject(connection, 413);\n        return 0;\n    }\n    total = header_length + (size_t)body_length;\n    while (received < total) {\n        ssize_t count = recv(connection, buffer + received, total - received, 0);\n\n        if (count < 0 && errno == EINTR) {\n            continue;\n        }\n        if (count <= 0) {\n            http_reject(connection, 400);\n            return 0;\n        }\n        received += (size_t)count;\n    }\n    (void)snprintf(id, sizeof(id), \"req-%lu\", sequence);\n    memset(out, 0, sizeof(*out));\n    out->connection = connection;\n    out->id = http_copy(id, strlen(id));\n    out->request.header = http_copy(buffer, header_length);\n    out->request.body = http_copy(buffer + header_length, (size_t)body_length);\n    if (out->id == NULL || out->request.header == NULL || out->request.body == NULL) {\n        free(out->id);\n        free(out->request.header);\n        free(out->request.body);\n        http_reject(connection, 500);\n        return 0;\n    }\n    return 1;\n}\n\nchar *http_render_header(const Response *response)\n{\n    static const char format[] =\n        \"HTTP/1.1 %d %s\\r\\nContent-Type: %s\\r\\nContent-Length: %zu\\r\\nConnection: close\\r\\n\"\n        \"Server: Wirecraft-WebServer/0.1\\r\\n%s\\r\\n\";\n    const char *type = response->content_type != NULL ? response->content_type : \"text/plain; charset=utf-8\";\n    const char *allow = response->status == 405 ? \"Allow: GET, HEAD\\r\\n\" : \"\";\n    size_t body = response->body != NULL ? strlen(response->body) : 0U;\n    int length = snprintf(NULL, 0, format, response->status, http_status_text(response->status), type, body, allow);\n    char *header;\n\n    if (length < 0) {\n        return NULL;\n    }\n    header = (char *)malloc((size_t)length + 1U);\n    if (header != NULL) {\n        (void)snprintf(header, (size_t)length + 1U, format, response->status,\n            http_status_text(response->status), type, body, allow);\n    }\n    return header;\n}\n\nint http_resolve(ReqRep *pending, ReqRep *resolved)\n{\n    const char *header = resolved->response.header;\n    const char *body = resolved->response.body;\n    size_t body_length = body != NULL ? strlen(body) : 0U;\n    int head = strncmp(pending->request.header, \"HEAD \", 5) == 0;\n    int status = 0;\n    char method[8] = \"\";\n    char path[128] = \"\";\n\n    if (header == NULL || http_write_all(pending->connection, header, strlen(header)) != 0\n        || (!head && body_length > 0U && http_write_all(pending->connection, body, body_length) != 0)) {\n        status = -1;\n    }\n    (void)sscanf(pending->request.header, \"%7s %127s\", method, path);\n    printf(\"%s %s %s %d %zu\\n\", pending->id, method, path, resolved->response.status, body_length);\n    (void)fflush(stdout);\n    close(pending->connection);\n    free(pending->id);\n    free(pending->request.header);\n    free(pending->request.body);\n    free(resolved->response.header);\n    free(resolved->response.body);\n    return status;\n}",
        "sourceLanguageId": "",
        "initialization": "",
        "initializationLanguageId": "",
        "specification": "HTTP/1.1 socket helpers lent as `libhttp` to socket_accept and socket_respond.\n- http_listen(port, any_address): non-blocking IPv4 listener with SO_REUSEADDR; 0 or -1.\n- http_wait(timeout_ms): 1 when a connection is ready to accept.\n- http_accept(sequence, out): accept one connection, read the header (≤ 8 KiB, up to the\n  blank line) and Content-Length body (≤ 64 KiB) with a 2 s timeout, then fill a ReqRep with\n  id \"req-<sequence>\", the connection and heap copies of header and body. Returns 1 for a\n  request, 0 when nothing was accepted or the connection was answered directly (408, 400,\n  413, 431, 500), -1 on a listener failure.\n- http_status_text(status): reason phrase.\n- http_render_header(response): heap-allocated response header; NULL on allocation failure.\n- http_resolve(pending, resolved): write header and (except for HEAD) body, print the access\n  log line, close the connection and free the strings each copy owns; 0 or -1 on write error.\n- http_close(): close the listener.\nWrites retry on EINTR and suppress SIGPIPE.",
        "specificationLanguageId": "markdown",
        "tests": "- A request split over several TCP segments is assembled before routing.\n- A 9 KiB header is answered 431 without entering the network.\n- A client that disconnects early does not terminate the server.",
        "testsLanguageId": "json",
        "aiInstructions": "",
        "aiInstructionsLanguageId": "markdown"
      },
      "binaryContent": null,
